## 6. Bed screw adjustment

The basic `SCREWS_TILT_CALCULATE` function is also available directly through the `Tools` section in Fluidd.

The `SCREWS_TILT` macro is a fully prepared version of the `SCREWS_TILT_CALCULATE` function. 
It homes the printer, heats the bed, heats the nozzle, and wipes the nozzle before starting. 
This helps ensure the nozzle is clean, which is important because the nozzle is also the bed probe.

The `Z_TILT` macro does a similar job, but includes homing, heating, and wiping 
for a smoother and more complete user experience than the stock function.

The "START_LUBRICATION" will drop the bed to the bottom and bring the extruder to the front and release the motors so making the cleaning and lubrication easy.
It will then with a push of a button go through a sequence to work the lubrication into the bearings, and at the end prompt you to wipe any access lubrication
off and the final button press will finish the sequence and reset the lubrication timer. 
In the "My_Calibration_Macro" file it is easy to adjust the accumulated time and the movement sequencies to your own requirements.
It will also show in the console, accumulated printing time before the next lubrication service required.

### Upgrade
Replacing the bed adjustment nuts and thumb nuts with nylock nuts and plain washers on each bed adjustment bolt 
which makes bed tramming much easier.

I also replaced the original bed springs with much stronger springs: Blue 16 OD x 8.5 ID x 15 mm. (the springs need to have a ID to accommodate a 4mm nut
These provide far more resistance when adjusting the bed.

